    basic: 'Try to win early tricks so you can declare trumps if you have a marriage. The first marriage declaration is crucial as it sets trumps for the whole hand.',
    intermediate: "Decide whether to declare your own marriage or ask partner. Declaring yourself gives 2 points and sets trumps immediately. Asking partner can be safer but 'breaks' your own marriages. Track which marriages have been 'broken'.",
    advanced: "The 'half marriage' declaration can be a clever tactic - it breaks all marriages in both hands, preventing opponents from declaring trumps later. Timing when to declare is key: too early and opponents know the trump suit; too late and opponent might declare first.",
    tips: [
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: 'If you have multiple marriages, you might declare a non-trump one first (if you can win another trick) for the extra game point',
      },
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: 'The last trick is worth 1 game point - fight for it, especially in close games',
      },
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: "If you're at 9 game points, focus on getting exactly 1 more - avoid the 'over 10' penalty",
      },
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: "Remember: you must beat your partner's card if you can, even if you'd rather let them win!",
      },
